Error --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- compatibility.js:3:9

Cannot assign `y` to `x` because in property `x`: `{bar: number, ...}` [1] is not exactly the same as
`{foo: string, ...}` [2]. [incompatible-type]

The above-mentioned two types must be the same because property `x` is invariantly typed. To fix the error,
- Either make `{x: {bar: number, ...}, ...}` [3] and `{x: {foo: string, ...}, ...}` [4] exactly the same
- Or make property `x` in `{x: {foo: string, ...}, ...}` [4] readonly. See
https://flow.org/en/docs/faq/#why-cant-i-pass-a-string-to-a-function-that-takes-a-string-number.

   compatibility.js:3:9
   3|     x = y; // 2 errors: `foo` not found in y.x; `bar` not found in x.x
              ^

